"A useful comparison is a light switch versus the wiring behind a wall. The meridian is the wiring — the path along which influence travels, mostly hidden. An acupuncture point is like a switch: a specific, accessible spot where a person can interact with that hidden system to produce an effect, without needing to see or touch the wiring itself. Just as flipping a switch in one room can turn on a light in a completely different room, stimulating a point on the foot can be intended to affect an organ deep in the torso.": "75a5f7dc9ce4",
